## 6. Steering — project memory

Steering files live in `.claude/steering/*.md`. `csdd` imports them into
`CLAUDE.md` as `@`-references inside the managed block between
`<!-- csdd:steering:start -->` and `<!-- csdd:steering:end -->`, so they load as
**always-on project memory** on every interaction. Do not hand-edit that block —
`csdd steering create` / `csdd steering init` keep it in sync.

### Inclusion modes — advisory metadata

Each file carries an `inclusion:` value in its YAML frontmatter. Under Claude
Code every imported file loads always-on, so inclusion is **documentation of
intended scope**, not a runtime loading switch (there is no native conditional
loading of arbitrary markdown). Pick the value that best documents intent; the
validator still checks the frontmatter is well-formed.

| Mode | Documents | When to use | Frontmatter |
|---|---|---|---|
| `always` | foundational, load everywhere | product/tech/structure, security policies | `inclusion: always` |
| `fileMatch` | scoped to certain files | API conventions, framework-specific rules | `inclusion: fileMatch` + `fileMatchPattern: ["src/api/**/*", "**/*Controller.*"]` |
| `auto` | task-triggered intent | observability, performance, deployment | `inclusion: auto` + `name:` + `description:` |
| `manual` | niche, reference on demand | rarely used guidance | `inclusion: manual` |

### Commands

```bash
# always
csdd steering create security --inclusion always

# fileMatch (--pattern is repeatable)
csdd steering create api-conventions --inclusion fileMatch \
    --pattern 'src/api/**/*' --pattern '**/*Controller.*'

# auto (--description is required and is the trigger phrase)
csdd steering create observability --inclusion auto \
    --description 'Logging, metrics, tracing. Use when adding or modifying instrumentation.'

# manual
csdd steering create regulated-domain --inclusion manual
```

### What belongs / does not belong

| Goes in steering | Does **not** go in steering |
|---|---|
| Organizational patterns and the *why* | File listings, directory dumps |
| Architectural decisions with rationale | Implementation details derivable from code |
| Naming, imports, package conventions | Secrets, tokens, credentials, customer data |
| Security, testing, observability policies | Agent-specific tooling internals |

**Golden rule:** *if new code follows existing patterns, steering should not need updating.*

