## 8. Custom sub-agents — least privilege

Custom agents live at `.claude/agents/<name>.md` and define delegated, scoped roles (reviewer, debugger, security reviewer…).

```bash
csdd agent create code-reviewer \
    --description 'Read-only adversarial reviewer' \
    --tools Read --tools Grep

csdd agent create security-reviewer \
    --description 'No-write security review of the current diff' \
    --tools Read --tools Grep --tools Bash \
    --model sonnet
```

### Rules

- `--tools` is **repeatable** and defaults to `Read, Grep` (least privilege). Add tools only when the role truly needs them.
- `--model` is optional. Use a stronger model for architecture/security; cheaper for mechanical review.
- The more powerful the agent, the **smaller the scope** must be and the **larger the human review** must be.

### Common archetypes

| Agent | Tools | Used for |
|---|---|---|
| `code-reviewer` | `Read`, `Grep` | adversarial review of diffs |
| `security-reviewer` | `Read`, `Grep` | security findings, no writes |
| `test-writer` | `Read`, `Edit`, `Write` (scoped to tests/) | adding test coverage |
| `debugger` | `Read`, `Grep`, `Bash` | root-cause investigation |
| `docs-writer` | `Read`, `Edit` (scoped to docs/) | documentation maintenance |

